# every other token by its kind), generic-ness and `...` alike. Else what differs: 3 a parameter's
# type (`_dsq_k` its name token), 4 the return type, 5 the parameter count, 6 one generic, 7 a `...`.
# Each type is read as an annotation is (`_ty_norm_eq`, the impl-return check's comparator): `Box<i64>` IS `Box` and
# `>>` IS `> >`, as the guide's "by its resolved type" says — compared token by token they were "another type".
